      'help.q1': 'What is a project?', 'help.a1': 'A project combines sources (where posts come from — a website RSS feed or a social account) and destinations (where they go). Create a separate project for each website — queues and billing stay easy to follow.',
      'help.q2': 'How much does SEOlit cost?', 'help.a2': '800 ₽ per 30 days per project. The plan includes one account in every network and unlimited feeds. Each extra network account is 100 ₽ per 30 days. The first 3 days are free.',
      'help.q3': 'How do I connect my website’s RSS feed?', 'help.a3': 'Open the project → “Sources” → “+ Connect” → “RSS/Atom feed” and paste the feed address. You can test the feed first in “RSS check”.',
      'help.q4': 'How do I connect a network to publish to?', 'help.a4': 'Open the project → “Destinations” → “+ Connect”, pick the network, sign in and choose the page or group.',
      'help.q5': 'What does “Sign in again” mean?', 'help.a5': 'The network revoked access — for example, after a password change. Press “Reconnect” on the destination row and sign in again; queued posts keep going out.',
      'help.q6': 'How do I limit posts per day?', 'help.a6': 'In “Schedules”, mark the publishing hours and a daily limit, then assign the schedule to accounts. Extra posts aren’t lost, they go out later.',
      'help.q7': 'How do templates work?', 'help.a7': 'A template builds the post text from the variables #TITLE#, #TEXT#, #URL#, #TAGS#. You can set a template per account in its settings.',
      'help.q8': 'What can the AI co-author do?', 'help.a8': 'It rewrites the post text by your instruction with Yandex GPT Lite / Pro and Llama 8B / 70B. You pay per token; one Lite token is 0.0002 ₽.',
      'help.q9': 'Is there a Bitrix24 integration?', 'help.a9': 'Yes, SEOlit is in the Bitrix24 app catalogue — link below.',
